     1	# Conformance Test Vector Schema
     2	
     3	This document defines the language-neutral schema for conformance golden vectors.
     4	Future implementations (e.g. loops-go) can prove semantic equivalence with the reference implementation by replaying these vectors.
     5	
     6	---
     7	
     8	## 1. Vector Envelope
     9	
    10	Every vector file is a single JSON document located at:
    11	`spec/conformance/vectors/<area>/<name>.json`
    12	
    13	### Envelope Fields
    14	
    15	| Field | Type | Required | Description |
    16	|---|---|---|---|
    17	| `name` | string | Yes | Short kebab-case identifier matching the file stem (e.g. `fold-key-string-projection-merge`). |
    18	| `description` | string | Yes | One sentence: what semantic decision this pins and why it exists. Must mention relevant decision tags when applicable. |
    19	| `input` | object | Yes | Area-specific input parameters. |
    20	| `expected` | object \| array \| primitive | Yes | The exact expected output after executing the input on the system under test. |
    21	
    22	### Envelope Example
    23	
    24	```json
    25	{
    26	  "name": "example-vector",
    27	  "description": "Pins a specific edge semantic under replay.",
    28	  "input": {
    29	    "spec": { ... },
    30	    "payloads": [ ... ]
    31	  },
    32	  "expected": { ... }
    33	}
    34	```
    35	
    36	---
    37	
    38	## 2. Area: `fold`
    39	
    40	The `fold` area pins the execution semantics of `atoms.Spec.replay`: given a Spec definition and an ordered sequence of fact payloads, it produces the exact accumulated final state.
    41	
    42	### `input` Schema
    43	
    44	| Field | Type | Required | Description |
    45	|---|---|---|---|
    46	| `spec` | Spec Object | Yes | The spec definition defining state fields and fold operations. |
    47	| `payloads` | array of objects | Yes | Ordered sequence of event payload dictionaries to replay. Payloads may include `_ts`, `ref`, and arbitrary application fields. |
    48	
    49	### `expected` Schema
    50	
    51	An object representing the final state dictionary. Every key in the dictionary corresponds to either a declared `state_fields` target, an auxiliary state key generated by a fold operation (e.g., `{target}_sum`, `{target}_count` for `avg`), or an error-rejection counter (e.g., `{target}_rejected`).
    52	
    53	---
    54	
    55	## 3. Spec Encoding
    56	
    57	A `Spec` defines data contracts and fold rules.
    58	
    59	### Spec Object
    60	
    61	| Field | Type | Required | Description |
    62	|---|---|---|---|
    63	| `name` | string | Yes | Unique identifier for the spec. |
    64	| `about` | string | No | Human-readable description (default: `""`). |
    65	| `input_fields` | array of Field Objects | No | Input field declarations (default: `[]`). |
    66	| `state_fields` | array of Field Objects | Yes | State field declarations. |
    67	| `folds` | array of FoldOp Objects | Yes | Ordered fold transformations to apply to incoming payloads. |
    68	
    69	### Field Object
    70	
    71	| Field | Type | Required | Description |
    72	|---|---|---|---|
    73	| `name` | string | Yes | Field identifier. |
    74	| `kind` | string | Yes | Type name: `"str"`, `"int"`, `"float"`, `"bool"`, `"dict"`, `"list"`, `"set"`, `"datetime"`. |
    75	| `optional` | boolean | No | Whether the field may be absent (default: `false`). |
    76	
    77	---
    78	
    79	## 4. Fold Operations (`FoldOp`)
    80	
    81	Each fold operation is a JSON object with a discriminator field `"op"`.
    82	
    83	### `latest`
    84	Stores the timestamp `_ts` of the latest event. If `_ts` is missing or `null`, the payload is rejected and increments `{target}_rejected` (decision: `fold-off-type-skip-with-counter`).
    85	
    86	```json
    87	{
    88	  "op": "latest",
    89	  "target": "last_seen"
    90	}
    91	```
    92	
    93	### `count`
    94	Increments an integer counter in `{target}` on every payload.
    95	
    96	```json
    97	{
    98	  "op": "count",
    99	  "target": "events"
   100	}
   101	```
   102	
   103	### `sum`
   104	Adds numeric `payload[field]` to `{target}`.
   105	- If `field` is absent / `null`: silently skipped.
   106	- If `field` value is non-numeric or boolean: skipped, increments `{target}_rejected`.
   107	
   108	```json
   109	{
   110	  "op": "sum",
   111	  "target": "total",
   112	  "field": "amount"
   113	}
   114	```
   115	
   116	### `collect`
   117	Appends incoming payload to `{target}` (list).
   118	- If `ref` field is present on payload, it is parsed (comma-separated, whitespace-trimmed) into sorted unique `_refs` array on the stored entry.
   119	- If `max` > 0 and list length exceeds `max`, oldest items are dropped (bounded buffer).
   120	
   121	```json
   122	{
   123	  "op": "collect",
   124	  "target": "history",
   125	  "max": 100
   126	}
   127	```
   128	
   129	### `upsert`
   130	Inserts or updates an entry in `{target}` (dict) keyed by `payload[key]`.
   131	- **String projection** (`decision:design/fold-key-string-projection`): The key is projected using `str(payload[key])`.
   132	- **Null key**: If `payload[key]` is `null` or missing, the payload is skipped.
   133	- **Merge default** (`decision:design/fold-merge-default`): New fields overlay existing entry fields; unmentioned prior fields persist.
   134	- **Observation count `_n`**: Incremented on each upsert for the key.
   135	- **Ref accumulation**: If `ref` is present on payload, comma-separated tokens are accumulated into `_refs` (sorted list of unique tokens across all upserts for this key).
   136	
   137	```json
   138	{
   139	  "op": "upsert",
   140	  "target": "users",
   141	  "key": "id"
   142	}
   143	```
   144	
   145	### `top_n`
   146	Maintains a dictionary in `{target}` with top `n` items ranked by numeric `by` field, keyed by `payload[key]`.
   147	- Key is string-projected (`str(key)`).
   148	- If `key` or `by` is absent / `null`: silently skipped.
   149	- If `by` is off-type (non-numeric / bool): skipped, increments `{target}_rejected`.
   150	- Ties preserve insertion order under stable sort.
   151	
   152	```json
   153	{
   154	  "op": "top_n",
   155	  "target": "leaderboard",
   156	  "key": "player",
   157	  "by": "score",
   158	  "n": 10,
   159	  "desc": true
   160	}
   161	```
   162	
   163	### `min`
   164	Tracks minimum numeric value in `{target}`.
   165	- Replaces initial `null` with first valid number.
   166	- Non-numeric / boolean values increment `{target}_rejected`.
   167	- Missing fields are silently skipped.
   168	
   169	```json
   170	{
   171	  "op": "min",
   172	  "target": "coldest",
   173	  "field": "temp"
   174	}
   175	```
   176	
   177	### `max`
   178	Tracks maximum numeric value in `{target}`.
   179	- Replaces initial `null` with first valid number.
   180	- Non-numeric / boolean values increment `{target}_rejected`.
   181	- Missing fields are silently skipped.
   182	
   183	```json
   184	{
   185	  "op": "max",
   186	  "target": "warmest",
   187	  "field": "temp"
   188	}
   189	```
   190	
   191	### `avg`
   192	Tracks incremental running average in `{target}`.
   193	- Maintains hidden state keys `{target}_sum` (float) and `{target}_count` (int).
   194	- Off-type values increment `{target}_rejected` and do not bump `{target}_count`.
   195	- Missing fields are silently skipped.
   196	
   197	```json
   198	{
   199	  "op": "avg",
   200	  "target": "mean_latency",
   201	  "field": "latency"
   202	}
   203	```
   204	
   205	### `window`
   206	Sliding FIFO window of field values in `{target}` (list).
   207	- Appends `payload[field]` to list.
   208	- If list length exceeds `size`, oldest values are dropped.
   209	- Missing fields are silently skipped.
   210	
   211	```json
   212	{
   213	  "op": "window",
   214	  "target": "recent_intervals",
   215	  "field": "interval",
   216	  "size": 10
   217	}
   218	```
   219	
   220	---
   221	
   222	## 5. Fact Encoding
   223	
   224	A `Fact` is an intentional observation with a routing kind, timestamp, payload, observer, and origin. In `replay` and `witness` vectors, facts are provided in append order as `[fact_id, Fact Object]` pairs.
   225	
   226	### `[fact_id, Fact Object]` Pair
   227	
   228	A 2-element JSON array: `[string, object]`
   229	- Index 0: `fact_id` (string) — 26-character canonical identifier (e.g. Crockford ULID).
   230	- Index 1: Fact Object (object) — serialized representation of the fact.
   231	
   232	### Fact Object
   233	
   234	| Field | Type | Required | Description |
   235	|---|---|---|---|
   236	| `kind` | string | Yes | Routing key matching the target spec (e.g. `"decision"`, `"item"`). |
   237	| `ts` | float | Yes | Unix epoch timestamp in seconds. Sub-millisecond precision is preserved. |
   238	| `payload` | object | Yes | Domain application payload dictionary. |
   239	| `observer` | string | No | Identifier of the producing observer (default: `""`). |
   240	| `origin` | string | No | Origin loop or vertex identifier (default: `""`). |
   241	
   242	---
   243	
   244	## 6. Area: `replay`
   245	
   246	The `replay` area pins store-level replay ordering on top of pure Spec folds.
   247	Given an append-ordered sequence of stored facts (which assign internal receipt ordinals / rowids), a conforming store replays facts filtered by kind strictly in **receipt order** (`rowid ASC`) — the order in which that store received them. The ULID `id` is stable identity only and `ts` is event-time metadata; neither orders the fold. `(ts, id)` survives only as an explicit read-path lens (see §9, Area `lens`). Each fact payload is augmented with system metadata fields (`_ts`, `_id`, `_observer`, `_origin`) and folded into the spec.
   248	
   249	### `input` Schema
   250	
   251	| Field | Type | Required | Description |
   252	|---|---|---|---|
   253	| `spec` | Spec Object | Yes | The spec definition defining state fields and fold operations. |
   254	| `facts` | array of `[fact_id, Fact Object]` | Yes | Sequence of facts in APPEND order (store insertion order). |
   255	
   256	### `expected` Schema
   257	
   258	An object representing the final accumulated state dictionary after full replay in receipt order (`rowid ASC`).
   259	
