    10	classifier, pinning the seven §07 rows with no journal encoding at all — §B.3's
    11	journal is a local cache grammar, not wire, and no other implementation is
    12	obliged to have one. ``form: "journal"`` hands raw lines to the pure reader and
    13	then attempts the comparison, because every read rule (trust-epoch scoping, the
    14	maximum-ordinal rule, equivocation, the incomplete-read lower bound, the
    15	header's three-way classification) is unreachable from the classifier.
    16	
    17	**Outcome strings, never exception types.** A vector names an outcome by its
    18	ratified §07 string. The one place a vector must speak of a refusal — a journal
    19	that equivocates — it names the READ STATE ``"equivocation"``, and the mapping
